# You almost certainly need NOTHING in here.
#
# The Sand Pavilion runs completely with no configuration at all: the Library
# reads from the bundled src/game/data/seed.js, everything you add lives on
# your own machine, and the app makes zero network requests. Copy this file to
# .env.local only if you specifically want one of the things below, and leave
# it absent otherwise. A missing .env.local is the normal, supported case.
#
# STANDING DECISION, 2026-07-12: this project is moving OFF Supabase and toward
# a local, self-hosted stack — local Postgres and local MinIO, no cloud account
# required for anything (plans/SELF-HOSTED-STACK-PLAN.md). The variables below
# are a leftover from before that, kept only because the code path still exists
# and still works. Do not build anything new that requires them.

# --- Optional, legacy: a hosted catalog + the two café boards ---------------
# Without these the Library uses the bundled seed and the café's two wall
# boards stay dormant, which is exactly how every beta build ships. Nothing
# else changes and nothing breaks.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# NEVER put a SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY in this file or in .env.local. It
# bypasses every row-level security rule in a project and is a different class
# of credential from the publishable key above. The one script that needs one
# (tools/caravan/promote-draft.py, a maintainer-only path into the shared
# catalog) reads it from an environment variable set in a single terminal
# session. See PROTOCOLS.md, Protocol 1, Pathway B.
